const BIOS = {"bill-chang": ["Bill Chang is currently serving as Chief Executive Officer & Executive Director of the Data Centre Business Unit and also Singtel’s new standalone infrastructure unit, Digital InfraCo, as of 1 June 2023. Prior to that, Bill joined Singtel in November 2005 as Executive Vice President of Corporate Business and subsequently became Managing Director, Business Group. He became CEO, Group Enterprise on 16 July 2012 and assumed the role of CEO, Regional Data Centre Business and Digital InfraCo unit.", "Bill is the Chairman of the Singapore Institute of Technology’s Board of Trustees and a board member of the Urban Redevelopment Authority of Singapore. He is also a member of the Australian Institute of Company Directors’ International Advisory Technology Governance and Innovations Panel. He co-chaired the Future Jobs and Skills Sub-committee of the Committee on the Future Economy of Singapore from 2016 to 2017."], "ahmad-fairus-rahim": ["Ahmad Fairus holds a Bachelor of Accounting (Honours) degree from Multimedia University, Cyberjaya. He is a Chartered Global Management Accountant (CGMA) and a Fellow of the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants (FCMA). He has also completed executive leadership programs at INSEAD Business School, International Institute for Management Development (IMD), and the ICLIF Executive Education Center.", "With over 20 years of experience delivering high-quality commercial finance and accounting support within the telecommunications industry, Ahmad Fairus brings a blend of financial expertise and strategic insight to his role. His extensive background encompasses long-term strategic planning, merger and acquisition and corporate restructuring, commercial partnership evaluations, and capital allocation to drive business growth. He first joined TM in 2001 and rejoined the company in 2018 as General Manager of Financial Planning and Analysis. Following this, he served as the Group Financial Controller before being promoted to Deputy GCFO in April 2024. He was appointed as the Group Chief Financial Officer of TM, effective 1 November 2024.", "Ahmad Fairus also contributes as a board member across several TM subsidiaries."], "nik-azli-abu-zahar": ["Nik Azli was appointed as the Group General Counsel effective 1 October 2022. He holds a Bachelor of Laws (Honours) from University of Newcastle Upon Tyne, United Kingdom. He has attained the Certificate of Legal Practice, Malaysia and was called to the High Court of Malaya as an Advocate and Solicitor.", "Nik Azli has extensive experience as an in-house legal counsel, where he has been part of the leadership team of several prominent organisations. Prior to joining TM, Nik Azli held several pivotal positions at companies such as Sapura Energy Berhad and Malaysia Airlines Berhad with notable and commendable achievements.", "Whilst practicing law, he was one of the advisers for several multinational companies in commercial transactions and energy and utility projects, including overseas transactions and projects spanning from China to the Middle East.", "He was also one of the recipients of the Energy and Resources In-House Legal Team Award at the prestigious Asia Legal Business (ALB) Malaysia Law Awards in 2015. In 2023, he was recognised and enlisted in the Legal 500 GC Powerlist Malaysia 2023."], "lee-yoong-kin": ["Lee Yoong Kin is currently serving as Chief Operating Officer of Nxera. Yoong Kin manages the data centre product function regionally and is responsible for product development and pricing, as well as driving branding and marketing. He is also responsible for setting up the organisation’s regional data centre operations and ensuring operational excellence and standardisation across the data centres.", "Yoong Kin brings with him more than 30 years of senior business and operational knowledge in the DC and ICT industries, including P&L, business development, sales and project experiences in multiple regions, such as Indonesia, Malaysia, Vietnam, Philippines, Thailand, China, and Hong Kong.", "Before joining Singtel, Yoong Kin was SVP/Group MD of Enterprise Business Group in TeleChoice International, where he was responsible for the profitability, growth and strategic direction of the business. He was also previously a Managing Director of Equinix Singapore Pte Ltd, which he co-founded in 1999, and General Manager and Board member of ST Teleport Pte Ltd (a subsidiary of ST Telemedia), which he set up in 1994.", "Yoong Kin holds a Bachelor of Engineering in Electrical & Electronic Engineering (First Class Hons) and an MBA from the National University of Singapore."], "mahathir-said": ["Holds a Bachelor of Engineering (Hons) in Electrical & Electronic from Imperial College London and a Master of Science in Information Technology from Universiti Teknologi MARA (UiTM). He has completed executive leadership programs at Oxford University, the International Institute for Management Development (IMD), and Cranfield University.", "With over 20 years of experience in IT operations, cloud services, and enterprise infrastructure, he has led end-to-end delivery of SAP ERP rollouts, enterprise architecture, DC migrations, and large-scale cloud and analytics projects, bridging strategic foresight with operational excellence.", "His past leadership roles include Vice President of Cloud Services at Credence (TM Digital Innovation Sdn Bhd) and Head of Professional Services at TM One, where he spearheaded major transformation initiatives across both public and private sectors. As Vice President of DC Business at TM, he played a pivotal role in expanding TM’s DC portfolio.", "Presently, the Chief Executive Officer (CEO) of TM Nxera, where he leads the build-out of a cutting-edge hyperscale DC in Iskandar Puteri, Johor."], "benedict-kwok": ["Benedict Kwok is the Country Manager for Malaysia at Nxera and the Chief Operating Officer of TM Nxera, a joint venture between Telekom Malaysia and Nxera. He leads the development and operations of hyperscale, AI-ready data centre infrastructure in Malaysia, overseeing multi-disciplinary functions spanning data centre operations, business management, facility management, and quality assurance.", "With over 25 years of experience in the digital infrastructure and telecommunications sectors, Benedict brings a strong blend of operational depth and strategic leadership. Prior to his current roles, he held leadership positions at NTT, where he drove regional growth, partnerships, and infrastructure development initiatives across Southeast Asia.", "Benedict has a proven track record in cost optimisation and business transformation, including revitalising operational resources following organisational carve-outs and establishing scalable frameworks to support market expansion. His experience spans multiple markets, including Singapore and Cambodia, providing him with a nuanced understanding of regional business environments and stakeholder dynamics.", "Fluent in three languages, Benedict is recognised for his adaptability and execution focus. He has also led entrepreneurial initiatives, including the launch of MobileBus under MobileOne, reflecting his ability to translate strategy into tangible outcomes.", "He holds professional qualifications in Business Management and Data Analytics & Artificial Intelligence, and is currently pursuing an Executive MBA, expected to be completed in mid-2026."], "aiguo-han": ["Holds a Bachelor of Engineering (Hons) in Electrical & Electronic Engineering from Nanyang Technological University.", "With over 12 years of experience in enterprise ICT services, he has served multinational, regional and local corporations with a range of roles spanning Product Management, Bid Management, to Global Account and Sales Management. He has a strong track record in stakeholder engagement, executive client relationship building and executing effective sales strategies.", "Presently, the Chief Commercial Officer (CCO) of TM Nxera, where he leads the commercial functions, including sales, marketing, partnerships and customer success. In this role, he is responsible for driving customer acquisition and revenue growth to meet the company’s strategic business goals."], "zuraida-hussain": ["A Chartered Accountant registered with the Malaysian Institute of Accountants (MIA), holding a Bachelor of Accounting (Honours) degree from the International Islamic University Malaysia (IIUM).", "Over 25 years of comprehensive experience in the field of finance, with a strong track record in strategic planning, mergers and acquisitions, corporate restructuring, and subsidiary management.", "Presently, the Chief Financial Officer (CFO) of TM Nxera, where she oversees cross-functional teams across financial planning & analysis, budgeting, investment strategies, and compliance to support the company’s data center growth and operational excellence."]};
